  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Choose the viewport",
      "items": [
        "Calendar: school dates and events. Layout: campus and venue views.",
        "Roster: absence, relief, timetables and notices. Deploy: staff and venue plans. Contacts: people and access."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Read once; use locally",
      "items": [
        "Load the usable Roster shell first. Transfer baseline content, then permitted suspended content for today plus 30 days.",
        "Keep decoded immutable content in IndexedDB. Check tags on the first Singapore-day load, hourly at :20, and once after a missed check.",
        "Matching tags need no timetable payload or decode. A cache does not grant access or confirm a save."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Save, publish, send",
      "items": [
        "Save to online commits the shared plan. Let teachers see releases its dated snapshot. Send WhatsApp creates eligible notification work.",
        "Each mutable store has its own authoritative owner. Independent projects do not share an Apps Script lock.",
        "Stable request IDs and durable receipts make a lost-response retry safe. SMC-touched allocations stay protected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Separate background work",
      "items": [
        "Notification, Inbox ingestion, planning, reports and optional Calendar continuation run as bounded tasks.",
        "D1 holds webhook jobs and read-build claims only. R2 holds private derived copies and media. Google retains school record authority.",
        "A signed webhook is accepted after durable receipt storage when enabled. Duplicate events reuse IDs; uncertain sends stay uncertain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Limits and recovery",
      "items": [
        "Roster still replaces its operational Drive JSON at commit. Logical changed fields are not SQL row isolation. Inbox still shares Roster ScriptLock.",
        "Calendar releases its lock for Google calls. Settlement checks the claim and source; a newer edit remains pending.",
        "Keep the original request, draft and reference after a timeout. A sent email closes a matching alert, not the underlying failed WhatsApp outcome."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Install and verify",
      "items": [
        "Use five Pages ZIPs, four gCodes and one complete notification Worker text file. Follow the separate maintainer guide for dashboard steps.",
        "D1 ingestion, R2 snapshots and Calendar continuation need their documented bindings and flags. Core paths remain available when optional features are off.",
        "This map describes release source, not a live configuration or measured delivery guarantee. No new Durable Object or Workflow is required."
      ]
    }
  ]
